hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16063","Affan narrated to us, Aban al-Attar narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Ubayd, that he cooked for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a pot in which was meat, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hand me its foreleg. So I handed him, and he said: Hand me its foreleg. So I handed him, and he said: Hand me its foreleg. So he said, O Prophet of Allah, how many forelegs has a sheep. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, had you been silent, it would have given you a foreleg whenever you called for it."
